    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d231">

                <pb facs="0317" n="233" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg233"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 862.20219/55</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Panama</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Price</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 390</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 21, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your No. 1388
                    of May 15, 1917, confidential, enclosing a copy of a note from the Panaman
                    Foreign Office forwarding a complaint of the Consul of Sweden, accredited to
                    Panama, concerning the internment of Oscar W. Eliassen with the Germans at
                    Taboga Island.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d231-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>In reply I have to say that you are authorized to advise the Panaman Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs that this Government will hold <pb facs="0318" n="234"
                        xml:id="pg234"/> Panama harmless against loss on account of having
                    heretofore interned persons in conformity with this Government’s desire,
                    provided this Government shall be kept informed of the proceedings of claimants
                    and be satisfied that the Government of Panama resisted their claims in good
                    faith.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
